Trading rules. 

Conditions : 
1. Take previoud day ATR and upper limit is
     (a) Upper_Limit = Previous day close + ATR 
     (b) Upper_Limit_80 = 80% of Upper_Limit
     (c) Lower_Limit = Previous day close - ATR 
     (d) Upper_Limit_80 = 80% of Lower_Limit
2. on 15 Min candle create 3 period EMA  and 22 period EMA 
3. Only Bull Put spread and Bear Call spread are supposed to be taken in this strategy 

Action : 

Entry conditions: 
*** Only One open Trade at time ***

First Trade entry :
  C. When 9:15 AM candle closes above Upper_limit_80 wait for a candle to touch ATR line and a RED candle  to take Bear Call Spread
  D. When 9:15 AM candle closes Below Lower_limit_80 wait for a candle to touch ATR line and a green candle to take a Bull Put spread call
  E. When 9:15 candle open in between  Upper_limit_80 and lower_limit_80 take a Bull Put Spread when lower length EMA crosses higher leangth EMA upwards
  F. When 9:15 candle open in between  Upper_limit_80 and lower_limit_80 take a Bear Call Spread when lower length EMA crosses higher leangth EMA downwards 

Susequent Trade entry :
  A. Bull Put Spread when lower length EMA crosses higher leangth EMA upwards, if there is reverse direction call close it and take new trade
  B, Bear Call Spread when lower length EMA crosses higher leangth EMA downwards , if there is reverse direction call close it and take a new call
  C. Bear Call spread Entry when Upper_Limit is touched , if there is no same direction call, if there is same direction call continue , if different direction call exit and take new call 
  D. Pull Put Spread entry when Lower_Limit is touched, if there is no same direction call, if there is same direction call continue , if different direction call exit and take new call

Exit conditions: 
A. If time is 3:15 PM or later, close all active positions 
b. If 3% target is acheived exit positions
c. Exit on reversal of EMA signal
----
🔧 Input Data Requirements
Previous Day:

Close Price

ATR (Average True Range)

Intraday:

15-minute candles (OHLC)

Real-time EMA(3) and EMA(22)

🔁 Definitions
Let:

prev_close = previous day's close

prev_atr = previous day's ATR

📈 Calculated Levels:
python
Copy
Edit
Upper_Limit = prev_close + prev_atr
Upper_Limit_80 = prev_close + 0.8 * prev_atr
Lower_Limit = prev_close - prev_atr
Lower_Limit_80 = prev_close - 0.8 * prev_atr
🔍 Strategy Conditions
✅ Indicators
3-period EMA and 22-period EMA on 15-minute candles.

⚠️ Rule: Only ONE open trade at any given time.
🟢 Entry Conditions
1️⃣ First Trade of the Day
Based on 9:15 AM candle (i.e., the first completed 15-min candle)

Condition	Action
Close > Upper_Limit_80	Wait for price to touch Upper_Limit AND see a Red Candle → Bear Call Spread
Close < Lower_Limit_80	Wait for price to touch Lower_Limit AND see a Green Candle → Bull Put Spread
Close between Upper_Limit_80 and Lower_Limit_80	If EMA(3) crosses above EMA(22) → Bull Put Spread
Close between Upper_Limit_80 and Lower_Limit_80	If EMA(3) crosses below EMA(22) → Bear Call Spread

🔁 Subsequent Trade Entries
(Only after the first trade is exited)

Signal	Action
EMA(3) crosses above EMA(22)	Close Bear Call if open → Open Bull Put
EMA(3) crosses below EMA(22)	Close Bull Put if open → Open Bear Call
Price touches Upper_Limit	If no Bear Call → Open Bear Call
If Bull Put open → Exit & open Bear Call
Price touches Lower_Limit	If no Bull Put → Open Bull Put
If Bear Call open → Exit & open Bull Put

🔚 Exit Conditions
Condition	Action
Time is 3:15 PM or later	Close all open trades
Net position achieves +3% profit	Close all positions
EMA crossover reverses	Close current position

